# Answer key for t2_depth.sql - B1 core SELECT, depth.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
#
# The test is that every fact below is the SAME fact T1 would give for the construct at
# the top level. Renaming and nesting change no edge; where they appear to, that is the
# finding.
#
# Influence COMPOSES along a path: a GROUP BY or window several levels down influences
# whatever the aggregated or windowed value finally lands in.
#
# FLAGGED, NOT LABELLED: S5's `WHERE g.gset = 1` filters on GROUPING(), i.e. on the
# grouping-set structure rather than on any column's data. No convention exists; nothing
# is labelled or forbidden for it (same treatment as T1 S10a).

@ 23 S1 alias chain, five levels
value customers.id -> top_customers.customer_id identity
value customers.full_name -> top_customers.full_name identity
forbid value customers.id -> top_customers.customer_id derived | five renames compute nothing; the edge stays identity

@ 51 S2 window four levels down
value fct_order_line.product_key -> product_performance.product_id identity
value fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.period_month identity
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.running_revenue aggregated
influence fct_order_line.product_key, fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.running_revenue
filter fct_order_line.status -> product_performance

@ 84 S3 re-aggregation, two GROUP BYs on one path
value fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily.store_id identity
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> sales_daily.avg_order_value aggregated
value fct_order_line.order_id -> sales_daily.orders aggregated
influence fct_order_line.store_id, fct_order_line.order_id -> sales_daily.avg_order_value
note store_id groups at both levels; order_id only at the inner one, where it decides what each order_total is.
influence fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily.orders
note COUNT(po.oid) counts the inner grouping key; only the OUTER grouping is applied to an aggregate on this path.

@ 113 S4 HAVING three levels down, WHERE over an aggregate at the top
value orders.customer_id -> customer_summary.customer_id identity
value orders.id -> customer_summary.lifetime_orders aggregated
value orders.amount -> customer_summary.lifetime_value aggregated
influence orders.customer_id -> customer_summary.lifetime_orders, customer_summary.lifetime_value
filter orders.status -> customer_summary
filter orders.amount, orders.id -> customer_summary post
note amount: HAVING SUM(amount). id: the outer `WHERE t.n_orders >= 3` filters COUNT(o.id), so it acts after aggregation (D-6).

@ 141 S5 ROLLUP inner, GROUPING() filter outer
value dim_customer.region -> kpi_rollup.region identity
value dim_customer.segment -> kpi_rollup.segment identity
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> kpi_rollup.revenue aggregated
influence dim_customer.region, dim_customer.segment -> kpi_rollup.revenue
filter dim_customer.is_current -> kpi_rollup

@ 163 S6 a join inside a derived table, joined again outside
value orders.order_ts -> channel_mix.period_month derived
value orders.channel -> channel_mix.channel identity
value dim_store.region -> channel_mix.region identity
value order_lines.quantity, order_lines.unit_price, fx_rates.rate_to_usd -> channel_mix.revenue derived
forbid filter fx_rates.rate_date -> channel_mix | an ON clause is structural (D-5), even when its operand was computed one level down
forbid filter orders.currency -> channel_mix | an ON clause is structural (D-5), even when its operand was computed one level down

@ 191 S7 aggregate FILTER three levels down
value fct_shipment.carrier_id -> carrier_scorecard.carrier_id identity
value fct_shipment.transit_days, fct_shipment.delivered_date, fct_shipment.promised_date -> carrier_scorecard.on_time_pct aggregated
influence fct_shipment.carrier_id -> carrier_scorecard.on_time_pct
forbid filter fct_shipment.delivered_date -> carrier_scorecard | FILTER (WHERE) changes one aggregate's value, at any depth (D-10)

@ 211 S8 DISTINCT ON two levels down, feeding an aggregate
value orders.currency -> channel_mix.channel identity
value orders.customer_id -> channel_mix.orders aggregated
value orders.amount -> channel_mix.revenue aggregated
influence orders.currency -> channel_mix.orders, channel_mix.revenue
filter orders.customer_id, orders.updated_at -> channel_mix
note D-9: the DISTINCT ON key and its tie-breaker decide which order per customer survives into the aggregate.

@ 232 S9 a predicate five levels down, never projected
value payments.order_id -> top_customers.customer_id identity
value payments.amount -> top_customers.revenue identity
filter payments.method, payments.currency -> top_customers

@ 256 S10 a column carried up and dropped
value inventory_snapshots.snapshot_date -> sales_daily.sale_date identity
value inventory_snapshots.on_hand -> sales_daily.units identity
forbid value inventory_snapshots.reserved -> sales_daily.units | projected at depth 3 and 2 as unused_cost, never read by the level that writes
forbid filter inventory_snapshots.reserved -> sales_daily | carried, never compared to anything

@ 273 S11 a named window two levels down, used twice
value fct_order_line.order_line_id -> product_performance.product_id identity
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.prev_month_revenue derived
value fct_order_line.quantity -> product_performance.growth_pct derived
influence fct_order_line.store_id, fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.prev_month_revenue, product_performance.growth_pct

@ 290 S12 three sibling CTEs at three grains
value fct_order_line.customer_key -> customer_summary.customer_id identity
value fct_order_line.order_date -> customer_summary.last_order_date identity
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> customer_summary.lifetime_value aggregated
value fct_order_line.order_id -> customer_summary.lifetime_orders aggregated
value fct_order_line.unit_price -> customer_summary.avg_basket aggregated
influence fct_order_line.customer_key -> customer_summary.lifetime_value
influence fct_order_line.order_date -> customer_summary.lifetime_orders
influence fct_order_line.customer_key, fct_order_line.order_date -> customer_summary.avg_basket
forbid influence fct_order_line.order_date -> customer_summary.lifetime_value | by_customer groups by customer_key only; order_date is by_day's grouping
forbid influence fct_order_line.customer_key -> customer_summary.lifetime_orders | by_day groups by order_date only; customer_key is by_customer's grouping

@ 326 S13 a window over an aggregate three levels below it
value fct_order_line.order_date -> sales_daily.sale_date identity
value dim_store.region -> sales_daily.region identity
value fct_order_line.gross_amount -> sales_daily.gross_amount aggregated
influence fct_order_line.store_id, fct_order_line.order_date -> sales_daily.gross_amount
influence dim_store.region, fct_order_line.order_date, fct_order_line.gross_amount, fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily.rank_in_region
note region and order_date partition the rank; gross_amount orders it through the SUM; store_id and order_date decided what each SUM is.
forbid value fct_order_line.gross_amount -> sales_daily.rank_in_region | RANK's ORDER BY decides the rank; no part of the sum is in it (D-4)
